version: "2.0"
description: >-
  @a-company/gnomon-gui (spec §11; M1.10 slice 1) - the single-page app the
  kernel's loopback #web-endpoint serves as a hash-pinned bundle. Dependency
  light (no framework yet; React arrives with the Doodle canvas, §12.7);
  everything self-hosted, no runtime CDN loads (rule-6 CSP). scripts/build.mjs
  bundles src/main.ts with esbuild (gnomon-contracts inlined) into
  dist/bundle/{index.html, boot.js, styles.css, app.js}, hashes the tree
  (gnomon-bundle-tree:v1) and with --embed writes the generated
  packages/gnomon/src/kernel/web/gui-bundle.ts (opaque base64 + pin literal);
  --check (first step of `npm test`) fails when that file is stale.
  The transcript (core/store.ts lineItems) reads Claude's stream-json AND
  gnomon-local's lines (a message_end reply, a tool_execution_start tool
  line); a local-model session's replies are labelled "local model"
  (ui/app.ts agentLabel/backendWord; rows remount when the label changes).
  TD-2026-10-19-063: a session.open refused claude_binary_changed shows in
  the New session sheet (#gui-folder-field open-failed) in plain words with
  ONE key, Review re-pin card, that closes the sheet and focuses the kernel's
  pre-staged re-pin card (never decides); that card's allow reopens the sheet
  on the same folder and model with Open focused (founder field test
  2026-10-23); a claim-mismatch card renders its first line
  red and marks Deny as the default (focused) key.

components:
  gui-rules-view:
    description: >-
      8.0:rules-view (founder: see the list of rules, revert a bad call,
      toggle one for a time, one save; session 2026-10-23-gnomon-rules-view,
      Mika C1-C3). core/rules.ts (PURE): rulesStatusOf (status.rules,
      fail-safe), the staging reducers (stageOff with a kernel-clock preset,
      stageOn, stageRemove, unstage, discard, reconcile), saveCost / saveLabel
      ("Save · no Touch ID" when the batch only tightens, "Save · asks Touch ID
      or your Mac password once" when any rule turns back on), beforeClose and
      closePromptText ("3 changes not saved · Save · Discard"), applyRequest
      (ONE request.rules.apply), refusedResult (plain words + next:, every
      change stays staged), afterSave ("card waiting · Decide in the stack"
      when the same press could not decide the card), rulesBlock (grouped by
      repo with counts, newest first, filter above 12 rules, the empty state)
      and expiryToastOf ("rule back on: <rule>", 6 s). Staged rows are marked
      by word and weight, never amber; a removed row is struck with a keep
      key. ui/rules-block.ts paints the block (rule-row, rules-save-bar;
      design system .atelier/systems/gnomon/); ui/settings-sheet.ts routes
      its trusted presses and asks before closing with changes staged;
      ui/app.ts owns the staged state, saveRules (ONE log.append, then the
      same press decides the card allow), the three entry points (palette
      rules.open "Rules…", the mode menu's "Always rules…", the Always toast's
      "see Rules"), the expiry toast and a status re-read on rule rows.
      Preview fixtures rules-0/1/5/50/200, rules-off-open, rules-tighten,
      rules-staged, rules-close, rules-refused, rules-waiting (DEV hook
      devRulesState, dropped from the served bundle). Test:
      test/rules-view.test.ts.
  gui-session-rename:
    description: >-
      8.0:session-rename (founder ask: rename a session). core/rename.ts
      (PURE): renameRequest (log.append request.session.rename{hsid, name}),
      planRename (contracts normalizeSessionName preview: unchanged sends
      nothing, '' resets, a refused name is a notice), bindInlineRename
      (Enter saves, Esc cancels, blur saves, settles once). core/store.ts
      folds the kernel's session.renamed into SessionRow.name; sessionTitle
      shows the name (cut to 28), sessionFullTitle is the tooltip text,
      derivedTitle the placeholder; the transcript shows a "renamed" line.
      ui/app.ts: double-click the header title or press the pencil
      (#rename-btn, aria-label "Rename session") opens #rename-input
      (aria-label "Session name", value = the name, placeholder = the
      derived title); double-click or F2 on a session-list row renames it in
      place (the rail does not repaint while it is open); palette command
      session.rename "Rename session" (not in BLOCK_SAFE_COMMANDS). Trusted
      gestures only. The title tooltip shows the full title and the hsid.
      Test: test/rename.test.ts.
  gui-model-picker:
    description: >-
      Founder ask 2026-10-20 ("is there no way to change the model of what
      claude is in the tool?"). core/model-picker.ts (PURE): MODEL_CHOICES
      (contracts CLAUDE_MODEL_ALIASES + custom), openModelOf (route claude
      sends the alias/id or 'claude' for default; local/any unchanged),
      pickerProblem (contracts claudeModelProblem), the per-folder memory
      (localStorage gnomon.model.byFolder <= 64 folders + gnomon.model.last;
      a stored value failing the check is never restored), sessionModelOf
      (kernel rows only: the last session.model{outcome:switched}.to, else
      session.open.model), switchRequest = log.append{kind:
      request.session.model, payload:{hsid, model}}, switchConfirmText (the
      conversation continues, the prompt cache restarts, a larger model uses
      the plan faster; never says context is lost). ui/model-picker.ts (DOM,
      mounted once by app.ts): the "claude model" select + custom id field
      injected after #ns-model (hidden for the local route), the header chip
      (model + ▾ menu) after the backend in #chead-meta (founder 2026-10-23
      "default button when pressed does nothing": the menu opened inside
      .chead-l, whose overflow: hidden clips it, and every streamed row's
      header paint rebuilt the chip; now the same session's chip nodes carry
      data-model-chip and paintChatHead keeps them in place, rebuilding the
      parts around them, and the menu hangs from .pane-head.chead under the
      key, right after .chead-l in the DOM so Tab goes key → items → the next
      header key (Mika 2026-10-23); Esc or a click elsewhere closes it), the confirm sheet
      #model-switch-dialog that sends only once armed by a trusted click on
      its Switch key or a trusted Enter in its id field, recorded before the
      submit (Aegis L1; never the submit event's isTrusted), and the
      read-only Settings slot [data-gnomon-slot="session-model"]. Tests:
      test/model-picker.test.ts.
      8.0:model-switch wiring: sessionModelOf also folds
      session.model{reconciled} (model = to) and {timeout} (uncertain = to,
      kept until reconciled, never after the session ended: a timeout before
      or after session.exited is not shown unconfirmed, Aegis L2); modelChipText shows "model: switching…
      (unconfirmed)" and disables the ▾ meanwhile; sessionModelText feeds the
      Settings Permissions row `session-model` (readonly, slot
      session-model, settings.ts SettingsInput.sessionModel); store.ts
      sessionModelLine writes one transcript line per outcome. Preview
      fixture `model-switch` (preview/fixtures.ts).
    tags: [gui, model]
  gui:
    loop-cards: >-
      8.0:loops (gnomon-loops.md §3.1, §3.3; build step 2): the generic card
      renderer shows the loop-trust and loop-choice kinds; core/render.ts
      ROOT_CLASS_BY_KIND names loop-trust allow (no Approve without the kernel's
      verified root-rows node), the stamp names continue (CONTINUED) and stop
      (STOPPED). The Loops view is build step 13. Test: test/loop-cards.test.ts.
    root-rows: >-
      TD-2026-10-20-514 (Aegis C1e, G-ID-11): rootRowsOf verifies the card's root-rows node against contentHash;
      renderCard shows "This decision signs" in full and NO root-class key without it; GuiStore.rootMismatches
      flags a logged rowsDigest that is not the shown rows' digest; a notice when status.helper.batch is
      unavailable (helper < 1.8.0). Aegis M1: rootDecisions come from the HASHED detail and must cover the kind
      table; any root-rows node, or a root kind, without verified rows shows only deny/reject/withdraw.
      TD-2026-10-22-769 (Mika F3): rootRowLine renders a gnomon-root-local:v1 row (localRootRowLine: the config
      version, every endpoint with its server, base, model and who may use it, the runner folder, tree and node
      sha) and returns null on ANY field it cannot render (unknown keys, a non-loopback base, a cloud compat, more
      than 4 endpoints, a malformed pin), so the local.config card shows only deny. core/loops.ts: status.loops
      startRefused becomes one `refused-start` stack alert per loop ("■ <id> didn’t start", ×n since), gone when
      the kernel drops the refusal.
    fidelity-2: >-
      Design fidelity pass 2 (2026-10-20, comp .atelier/sessions/2026-10-15-gnomon-aesthetic/refs/direction.html).
      Cards (core/render.ts renderCard): "■ project · kind · by <name>" + the bordered voice chip, a title
      (one line for a kernel line 1; a composed permission title wraps, see fidelity-2-aegis), "raised HH:MM · waiting Nm", the keys, a quiet single-line contentHash (full hash in title=),
      then a `details` disclosure (details/summary allowlisted in h()) with the full requester + session,
      the kernel-composed body, and a requester's own words labelled as theirs. Always VISIBLE: the short
      requester (shortRequester: a local p:<ns>/<name> shows its name, a foreign or odd principal shows
      whole), the contentHash line, keys and flags, a held countdown, the ask picker, a claim-mismatch
      card's whole body. A permission title ("Allow Bash <command>") is composed by permissionTitleOf ONLY
      from the approval.request row's structured tool/tool_input (store StackCard.tool/toolInput),
      cross-checked against the kernel's line 1 and, when present, the contentHash-verified detail's
      inputHash (toolInputHash). Buried pile details are inert like buried keys. A stateless card's edge
      is its project's ink (pe-hN). Rail: one line per session, no project heading rows; voice attaches
      from the header pill menu only. Header: the connection readout is a quiet chip ("connected"; the
      identity in its title= and Settings → About), glyph-only theme switch, night keys without [ ] caps
      except + New session. Chat header: meta line kept whole, run mode as a compact kernel-owned 24px quiet key
      (modes.ts modeChip; board gnomon-chip: a key, never a chip), counts and raw toggle in a ⋯ menu. Transcript: session.open (not resumed) and
      voice.session.start are raw-only. Composer: one row, ⌘↵ hint, small send, the target/mode in title=.
      Stack head: "Stack · N · hover to fan" + a small filter key. Footer: an "Install Workshop" key,
      DISABLED with the CLI command in its tooltip because install has no GUI request kind
      (mod-panels.ts WORKSHOP_INSTALL_KEY; modhost/control.ts), and ONE quiet status line (detail in
      title=). Preview clock pinned to 14:07:10 (src/preview/env.ts PREVIEW_NOW).
    fidelity-2-aegis: >-
      Aegis BLOCK on fidelity pass 2 (2026-10-20). H1: a composed permission title never hides a
      command's tail. permissionTitleOf keeps the command's lines (no whitespace collapse; only the ends
      trimmed) and caps only at TITLE_ARG_MAX (4000 code points, `truncated: true`); renderCard's argEl
      puts each line in its own .card-arg-line with a visible ⏎ (.card-nl), marks ; && || | & ` $( as
      .card-sep, and the CSS wraps the composed title (pre-wrap, overflow-wrap: anywhere, no ellipsis).
      A capped arg adds a "longer than N characters" note and shows the kernel body VISIBLY, outside
      details (like a claim-mismatch card).
      L2: shortRequester(requestedBy, localNs) shortens only when the principal's namespace is the local
      trust set's (localNsOf the handshake principal, passed as CardView.localNs); else the principal shows
      whole.
      L3: a model-text choice chip keeps its filled choice-k pill at night too (two cues: dashed edge +
      pill), never the dashed border alone.
      L4: h() keeps `id` OFF its attribute allowlist (display data must not clobber getElementById); the
      reconnect close key sets .id after h() (the update banner is a #gui-toast now). approval.mode.set rows stay visible as a
      system line ("run mode a → b") and in the raw view.
    workshop-caps: >-
      S5 (critique 2026-10-20 §2 S5): the Workshop mod mounted as structured
      SVG caps. core/render.ts renderCap draws a Text node's `cap` only after
      contracts checkCap passes (else the text form shows): svg > path built
      with createElementNS (allowlisted tags svg/path, attrs viewBox/d/
      aria-hidden/focusable), path d from the GUI constant CAP_PATHS (tall/
      wide/floppy), colour by classes only (.hN fill + --key-edge ring,
      .outlined uses the hue ink, .knot violet), .bob only for state
      working, reduced motion prints `working`; the label shows above a
      needs/knot cap and the text is the aria-label. Text tones are the
      closed TONES set. Mod fences render Box titles. core/mod-panels.ts
      routes the workshop/workshop.strip sidebar view to its own `workshop`
      region (#workshop-host); app.ts applyLayout places it in the footer
      (#pane-workshop, default), the 76 px #workshop-col left or right, or
      hidden (Layout.workshop, persisted via serializeLayout in
      localStorage; always the footer under 900 px). workshopAbsence shows
      one quiet line when the Workshop is not running. The old shuttle
      readout is #status-line at the footer's right end (opens
      view.kernel-feed). The strip's line (founder report 2026-10-23): in the
      footer every word (mod label, zone titles, quiet notes, the paused line,
      the status line) sits in one --key-h line box at the strip's floor, so
      all baselines agree with each other and with the Install Workshop key;
      hats stand on that floor; nothing wraps. The preview's workshop fixtures
      name the mod gnomon.workshop (the S0b id the region routes on).
      Tests: test/workshop.test.ts.
    mod-panels: >-
      K0 mod panels (#ledger-mod host slice). core/mod-panels.ts (PURE):
      modPanelsOf(status) reads status.mods.views (the #mod-host declared
      views of running mods; the non-human status has counts only, so none)
      and maps slot to region: composer.footer -> desk footer (under the
      composer), sidebar -> bottom of the left (sessions) pane, panel -> the
      right (decisions) pane, below the kernel-owned stack. Every other slot
      (status.mod, tool.view:*, card.detail:*) and every kernel-owned region
      is never a mod slot. renderModFence wraps the kit renderer output in a
      <section class=mod-fence> labelled mod:<name> with a warn `dev` chip for a
      dev-linked (tier local) mod or a dev result; a refusal shows verbatim
      in the fence. ModPanelScheduler: re-render only on a LIVE store row of
      a MOD_FEED_KINDS kind (held equal to the kernel FEED_KINDS by test),
      debounced by MOD_PANEL_DEBOUNCE_MS, one render in flight (rows during it queue exactly
      one more), never on a timer. K3 (#paradigm-context-mod): mod.view input
      is {focus:{hsid}} only (the HOST joins it to the live session repo;
      the GUI never names a repo or path) and a focus change re-renders now
      (ModPanelScheduler.focus, app.ts focus() -> modPanelsFocus; closes
      T-2026-10-20-008 (4) for the Ledger). ui/mod-panels-mount.ts is the browser
      glue (creates the slot containers next to their panes, no index.html
      change, calls mod.view with input {hsid: focused} as display context);
      app.ts only calls mountModPanels after each attach's status read and
      feeds live rows to its hook. render.ts: Text tone -> class tone-<token>
      (the closed TONES, now with the kit's head and chip), Box direction row
      -> blk-row; a hue tone (hue-0..5) is the project's ■ swatch in the
      hue's ink pair (□ for a hollow mark), the chat header's, never a ringed
      dot. Fitted views (founder 2026-10-23, "these mods have terrible
      display"): every fence but the Workshop's renders with ctx.fit (body
      class mod-fit, an inline-size container): 11.5 body and 10.5 quiet,
      a 2px-grid rhythm, an id (no whitespace, > FIT_TOKEN_MIN) on one line
      with an ellipsis and its full text in title (never broken mid-token),
      row prose clamped to two lines and starting its own line after an id,
      and a Table fitted by tableFit (label-style heads, numbers right-aligned
      and tabular, cells capped at FIT_CELL_MAX with title, a width bucket
      tw-N from its natural width; one container query per FIT_TABLE_BUCKETS
      entry lays a narrower table out as its first cell over key-value
      pairs, empty cells left out, cells never wider than the column, 8px
      between rows). Truncated items are keyboard-reachable (Mika
      2026-10-23): markTruncated (core/mod-panels.ts) gives exactly the ids,
      cells and clamped titles the CSS cut one tab stop each (tabindex 0,
      full text in title), redone on render, column resize (ResizeObserver)
      and fonts loading; :focus-visible shows the whole text in a 2px
      --key-edge ring. A mod meter is ink on a --rule track.
      Generic: no mod-name case. test/mod-fit.test.ts. Aegis M2:
      the right-pane region is a sibling after #stack (outside its scroll),
      ruled off by a 2px --rule top border and headed `mods`; a block holding
      any kit.Button is refused in the panel slot (PANEL_BUTTON_REFUSAL shown
      in the fence). test/mod-panels.test.ts.
    self-update: >-
      TD-2026-10-19-063 restart (core/restart.ts, PURE but injected storage
      and fetch): a pending daemon-stop{reason:'upgrade'} card shows a
      persistent toast (#gui-toast) "Gnomon was updated · Restart now", whose key only focuses
      the card (the restart is the card's accept, one Touch ID). This page's
      own accept sets a single-use sessionStorage marker; the kernel's
      gui.resume{resumeToken, kernelPublicKey} (this connection only) is
      stored into that marker only. On close the page polls its origin
      (ORIGIN_POLL_MS cadence, ORIGIN_POLL_TRIES) and reloads; the reloaded
      page takes the marker once and attaches with {resumeToken}, re-pinning
      the successor key that came over the old verified channel. No answer:
      plain-language guidance (Gnomon.app, or `gnomon`).
    run-modes: >-
      P8-D86/D87 run-mode control (spec §11.4, §11.5): core/modes.ts (PURE)
      reads the focused session's mode ONLY from status.runModes (unknown
      values fail safe to manual), plans a choice (same | tighten | loosen |
      blocked with its ceiling reason), cycles ⇧Tab manual → ask →
      auto-edits → manual (skipping a blocked one) and builds the request
      log.append{kind:'request.mode.set', payload:{hsid, to} | {repo, to}}.
      ui/app.ts: a kernel-owned `mode: <mode> ▾` button + menu in the
      transcript header, ⇧Tab in the composer, palette mode.* (session) and
      mode.repo.* (repo), all on trusted gestures only (G-GUI-04); a
      loosening's pending strictness card is approved `allow` in the same
      gesture (the kernel asks for Touch ID), a refusal is shown as given;
      status is re-read when the store flags `modes` (approval.mode.set,
      request.mode.set, session.open, session.exited rows), never on a timer.
      mode.* commands are excluded from BLOCK_SAFE_COMMANDS. The transcript
      shows approval.auto as a subtle `auto-approved edit · <path>` line
      (`auto-approved · <tool> (always rule)` for a rule) and
      approval.mode.set as a system line. F2 (TD-2026-10-20-086): the
      switch, ⇧Tab and the menu default to FOLDER scope (the repo,
      labelled "this folder"; defaultScope/planFor/scopeEntries/SCOPE_LABEL,
      status repoMode) so a new session in the same folder starts in the
      chosen mode; "this session only" is the secondary entry (palette
      mode.*); a session that already has its own mode keeps session scope.
      F3: a folder on the root-signed default (status source 'config')
      is labelled `mode: auto-edits (default) ▾`. Tests: test/modes.test.ts.
    standing-feed: >-
      TD-2026-10-20-086 F6 (#standing-grant's GUI): core/standing.ts (PURE)
      reads status.standing fail-safe, turns grant.standing / .used /
      .revoked rows into feed lines (a use is also a toast naming what
      Gnomon did), decides the once-a-day offer (shouldOffer: a pending
      strictness/permission/voice-arm/daemon-stop card, no live
      grant, not offered today) and builds request.grant.standing{tuples,
      repos} / request.grant.standing.revoke{grantId}. ui/standing-feed.ts
      (its own module; app.ts only mounts it and forwards live rows and
      status reads) shows each use as an info toast on the page's one toast
      region (#gui-toast; no bottom-right toasts of its own; a window joining
      the unlock is a warn), today's list with Revoke (a tighten, no presence)
      and the offer as a persistent toast with one key, "Make it standing",
      which files the request on a trusted press and then focuses the grant
      card in the stack (founder decision with Aegis: a toast never decides a
      card; the person accepts it there, one password); its close key reads
      "Not today". Tests: test/standing.test.ts.
    voice-controls: >-
      Voice slice V2d (TD-2026-10-19-298, T-2026-10-19-026; spec §11.4
      header, §14.7 attachment). core/voice.ts (PURE): voiceStatusOf is the
      one adapter over status.voice (V1 nested {attached: {voiceSessionId,
      hsid, mode, turns} | null}; V2a flat {attached: boolean, hsid,
      ceiling: ptt | conversation | null (the attachment's state, not a
      cap), since, idleAt, voiceSessionId, turns, echoTailMs,
      ambientIdleMs}, optional clientConnected, hotkey, level, maxMode);
      V2a refusals voice-off (cause aec | ceiling | presence) and
      voice-playback read as plain lines (voiceRefusalNote); an undecided
      widen card (strictness, op voice.widen) is focused in the stack; an
      attached session whose mode is not ptt reads as ambient
      (the indicator never under-reports a live mic). Three states: Mic off
      (grey), push-to-talk (neutral ink2 since S1, never slate, "Hold <hotkey> to talk"), ambient
      (S1: amber warn-edge, static amber dot, "Listening", level meter that moves only on an audio event; vermilion only when crashed). clientConnected is
      only an explicit kernel field (null when unsure; no client-name
      guesses); attached with the app not connected keeps the attached
      state's class, label and meter plus "· voice app not connected"
      (never under-reports a live mic); "Voice app not running" only with
      nothing attached. pillOf(v, clientTail) appends the voice-app
      lifecycle's tail instead when the kernel reports one (see
      voice-app-lifecycle; T-2026-10-20-002), and an attached ambient pill
      keeps its warn colours under any client class (dashed edge).
      planVoice: same | free (Off, narrowing, re-target) | presence (the
      first widening to ambient in a GUI login) | blocked (ceiling, nothing
      focused). voiceRequest builds log.append voice.session.start{hsid,
      mode: ptt | conversation, continues?} or voice.session.end
      {voiceSessionId?}. canAttach: only a human-class connection (a voice
      connection never gets the controls). ui/app.ts: the kernel-owned
      header pill + menu (Off / Push-to-talk / Ambient, Attach to focused),
      [Voice ▾] on the focused live session row, palette voice.off /
      voice.ptt / voice.ambient, all on trusted gestures (G-GUI-04); a
      pending card from an ambient request is approved allow in the same
      gesture only when isVoiceWidenCard (kind strictness, detail.op
      voice.widen, the same hsid) holds for the card in the store; else it is
      focused in the stack (the kernel asks for Touch ID); the "decide the
      pending card in the stack" notice remembers that cardId and clears once
      the card has been seen in the store and is no longer pending (decided,
      expired or swept; cardNoticeStep, T-2026-10-20-002). Status is re-read when the
      store flags `voice` (voice.session.start / .end / .mode, daemon.start),
      plus the voice-app lifecycle poll (voice-app-lifecycle); voice.turn.* rows
      only kick the meter. The kernel's
      idle auto-off (voice.session.end with reason idle) is a warn toast
      (#gui-toast, 10 s; store.voiceToast idle, "Dictate turned off after N min idle" in
      ladder words, board header-5b); a new attachment drops one unshown. Transcript: a voice turn is the user message
      (one line, tagged with a mic and the speaker, capped at 32 chars) only
      when the kernel's turn.sent{source: voice, voiceTurnSeq} cites it;
      claude's replay of it shows once; until then the app's refusal /
      intercepted / forwarded claims are shown attributed ("voice app says:
      ..."); turn.sent adds its own line only when the voice row is
      unreadable, partials in grey while they are the latest word on their
      turn, a speaker marker under a spoken reply, a refused voice turn's
      reason inline and subtle. voice.* are excluded from
      BLOCK_SAFE_COMMANDS. Contrast: ambient text is the fixture's
      voice-armed pair (warn-ink on warn-bg), push-to-talk text the
      fixture's slate token; the pulse and meter stop under reduced motion.
      Tests: test/voice.test.ts; bundle pin in gnomon test/web-units.test.ts.
    voice-app-lifecycle: >-
      Voice slice V2e GUI (T-2026-10-19-026), SEAMLESS: no terminal step.
      core/voice-client.ts (PURE) is the one adapter over
      status.voice.clientConnected + status.voice.client {phase idle |
      installing | downloading | starting | running | crashed | unavailable,
      downloadMb {n, of}, devUnsigned, lastError, unavailable} and the
      enrolled list (status.voice.enrolled; absent = unknown, never a false
      nudge). Unknown phases fail toward not running.
      With nothing attached the pill shows "Voice app not running" [Start
      voice], "Setting up voice…", "Downloading voice models · N of M MB" with
      a progress bar, "Starting…", "Voice crashed" [Restart], "Voice
      unavailable · <why>", or (running, no enrolled voice) "Teach Gnomon your
      voice first" [Teach], or (every enrolled name has only a stale print,
      status.voice.prints.stale; enrolNudgeOf) "Re-teach Gnomon your voice
      (the voice check was upgraded)" [Re-teach]. Attached (T-2026-10-20-002), the live mic keeps
      its V2d class, label and meter and clientPillOf returns a `tail` that is
      appended (first match): crashed / backoff "· voice crashed: <lastError>"
      (one line, capped at 60 chars; title capped at 400) [Restart], the
      setup phases ("· setting up voice…", "· downloading voice models…",
      "· voice starting…"), "· voice unavailable: <why>", not connected "·
      voice app not connected" [Start voice], or enrolled [] "· teach Gnomon
      your voice first" [Teach] (enrolled null = unknown: no nudge). The
      kernel logs no row on a client phase or connection change, so the page
      re-reads status every 2 s (CLIENT_POLL_MS, one read in flight) while
      clientPollWanted: a human connection, a known lifecycle, and voice
      attached or the app installing / downloading / starting / in backoff. The pill
      menu adds Start / Restart / Stop voice and "Teach Gnomon your voice…";
      palette voice.client.start / voice.client.stop / voice.enrol (never
      block-safe). Gestures are trusted-only log.append rows from a human
      connection: request.voice.client{op: start | stop};
      attach or Ambient while the app is idle or crashed sends start first in
      the same gesture. A LOUD role=alert banner "Voice is running an unsigned
      development build" shows when devUnsigned is true. The enrolment dialog:
      name (kernel rule [a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,63}, normalized), plain consent
      text, request.voice.enrol{name, consent} (answer {pending, cardId} =
      the Touch ID card, A4), Confirm with Touch ID (approve allow) FIRST,
      then the three phrases one at a time with a recording indicator folded
      from status.voice.enrolment (A3: requested, ready, recording, recorded,
      done, failed; reports stamped before the allow are ignored), re-read on
      every status read plus a light 1 s poll only while the dialog waits;
      closing while the card is pending denies it; enrolled voices with a
      two-click [Forget] sending request.voice.forget{name} (no card).
      Notices are status.voice.notice{text, code?, at}: a new `at` is a
      warn toast (#gui-toast) prefixed "Voice app: ", never a decision or a backlog
      replay (30 s). Aegis L2-L4: the dev-unsigned banner is a persistent
      alert (no timer); "done" shows only once status.voice.enrolled lists
      the name; during the phrases the dialog says "Recording <name> — only
      <name> should speak"; isEnrolCard requires the card to name the voice.
      The kernel's client phases (stopped, preparing, installing,
      downloading-models, starting, running, backoff, failed, unavailable)
      map onto the pill's (downloadMb may be a total in MB). Kernel
      replies voice.turn.agent{source: kernel-speakable, items} show the
      speaker marker and swallow the voice app's next playback row (never
      shown twice). Tests: test/voice-client.test.ts.
    journal-cursor: >-
      Slice A4 (P8-D98): the hello offers journal.cursor; core/client.ts
      followLog pages then follows with the store's {logId, seq} cursor
      (GuiStore.cursor/advance/adopt); on BAD_REQUEST{cursor-epoch} (or a
      page from another log) GuiStore.reset() clears every row-derived
      state and the read starts over from the current log (once; a second
      refusal surfaces). Tests: test/gui.test.ts (journal.cursor).
    wire-rows: >-
      Dogfood fix 2026-10-19: core/store.ts rowOf flattens each log.read
      row as the kernel sends it (contracts LogRow: {seq, view:'full',
      event} | {seq, view:'stub', stub:{kind, hsid?, at}} | {seq,
      view:'oversize', kind, bytes}) before the reducers read kind, session
      and payload; reading the nested row flat left every row in the kernel
      feed (no session list, no transcript, and a TypeError painting the
      feed). turnEventSummary renders a turn.event line as the assistant
      text, its tool names and the result subtype. The composer says why
      nothing was sent (no session focused / not connected) instead of
      returning silently. Tests: test/gui.test.ts (wire rows, turn.event
      lines); the real-kernel falsifier is gnomon
      test/gui-session-e2e.test.ts; bundle pin in gnomon
      test/web-units.test.ts.
    session-resume: >-
      T-2026-10-19-014 B2 (§2.4 rule 11): the hello also offers
      session.resume (send/stop on a session the kernel resumed after an
      upgrade). GuiStore drops every card it holds on a new daemon.start row,
      so an old kernel's card id is never clickable (the new kernel refuses it
      NOT_FOUND and retires it with approval.expire). Tests: test/gui.test.ts
      (#gui store after an upgrade); bundle pin in gnomon test/web-units.test.ts.
    materials-s1: >-
      S1 papercraft/phosphor materials (critique 2026-10-20 §2 S1, Luna).
      Self-hosted fonts in static/fonts/: JetBrains Mono 400/500/600 and one
      Fraunces variable cut (opsz + wght, covers 460 and 600), Fontsource
      5.3.0 latin subsets copied unmodified, each family with its OFL 1.1
      licence beside it (OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt, OFL-Fraunces.txt; no
      Reserved Font Name upstream); @font-face font-display swap, font-src
      'self', no CDN, no data: URL. scripts/build.mjs walks static/
      recursively: .html/.css/.js/.svg/.txt get LF, everything else (woff2)
      is read raw; *.woff2 is binary in .gitattributes. Bundle files may sit
      in sub-directories (fonts/...); the kernel materializes them under
      <home>/gui/bundle/ and serves woff2 as font/woff2. Tests:
      test/fonts.test.ts (pinned sha256, embed byte-exact, licences, CSS
      sources), ../gnomon/test/gui-endpoint.test.ts (served byte-exact).
      scripts/preview.mjs (dev only) serves grain.svg and fonts/* raw too.
    desk-structure-s2: >-
      S2 desk structure (critique 2026-10-20 §2 S2). Pure helpers in
      core/store.ts: groupHue (projectHue of the session.open cwd, else of the
      repo: the SAME function as the kernel's Workshop feed), sessionTitle (the
      first user message cut to 28 chars, else repo basename · hsid tail 4;
      SessionRow gains cwd, openedAt, firstUser), sessionNote (N card(s) /
      KNOT in warn ink, failed in vermilion), splitActivePast, failedExit (a
      session.exited with reason error, or no stop reason and a non-zero code
      or a signal, is state "failed", terminal), foldActivity +
      activitySummary + durationText (consecutive tool / auto rows fold into
      ONE collapsible activity line "HH:MM–HH:MM · read N files · ran N
      commands · Ns of work", key act:<first key>; a reply after a user
      message gets "took Ns"). core/render.ts mdInline / mdBlocks: a SAFE
      markdown subset for agent text (inline code, bold, italics, bullet and
      numbered lists, fenced code) built as DOM nodes through h(); no HTML
      passthrough, no links, no images. ui/app.ts: the rail is ACTIVE n
      (project groups: swatch + project ink name) and ▸ PAST n (collapsed by
      default, toggle kept in localStorage gnomon.gui.pastOpen; a failed session stays in ACTIVE); the kernel
      feed is a palette view (view.kernel-feed), the default centre is a
      quiet "No session open" sheet with + New session; the chat header is
      the session name plus ■ project · backend · started · elapsed; pinned
      cards carry "Pending in this session"; the header (board header-5b,
      #gui-wordmark-menu) is the wordmark menu, the palette field, spacer,
      the link dot + risk chip, the voice pill (Layout presets and pane
      toggles live in the Gnomon menu; kernel-owned chrome is never listed); #inbox
      sits in the stack head; the composer placeholder is "Reply to <name>…"
      with the long hint in title=, and send is the filled primary key.
      Tests: test/desk.test.ts.
    card-sheet-pile-s3: >-
      S3 card sheet and stack pile (critique 2026-10-20 §2 S3). renderCard
      anatomy (data only from kernel fields): header ■ <repo basename> in
      the project ink (the ONE hue, groupHue) · kind · the voice tag from
      the kernel's card.voice (🎙 reversible · <label>, 🎙 gate + the
      .handle word, else hand only), requestedBy and the session in title=;
      the title (the block's first Text line, splitCardBlock; a
      claim-mismatch card keeps its block whole and is titled by its kind);
      the body (kernel-owned); "raised HH:MM · waiting Nm" (raisedLine, from
      the approval.request row at, StackCard.raisedAt); keys; .bar and
      .stamp (S4 animates them); the contentHash line last. CSS: a sheet with
      a --edge-w state edge on the left (knot / failed / gate-class + held /
      claim-mismatch; a neutral card's edge is --key-edge, never --rule) and
      --sheet-shadow (night: a 1px --rule ring, no shadow). The stack is a
      pile: -64px overlap, rotation and z-order by :nth-child classes (no
      inline style), fanned flat on :hover AND :focus-within (keyboard
      reach) and .fan / .open; more than 6 cards ⇒ 6 piled + "+n more"
      (opens the fanned pile); pinned cards lie flat. The pane head reads
      Stack · n pending · hover to fan · scope key; rail minmax(300px,340px).
      The preview (dev only) takes ?fan=1. Tests: test/desk.test.ts.
    motion-s4: >-
      S4 motion (critique 2026-10-20 §2 S4; founder 2026-10-23). Arrival is a
      quick fade-in, opacity only (card-in on the --t-arrive motion token; no
      flutter), at the pile rotation; the stamp lands straight; a pinned card
      takes one of four preset tilts (.r-a..d by cardId; never inline
      style). Approve: ONLY after the kernel accepted the decision (a
      refusal throws first), fadeOff stamps APPROVED (--ink; board gnomon-status-colour), adds
      .out after a fixed stamp hold: a fade-out, opacity only (card-fade on the --t-fade motion token, design-system tokens.motion; founder 2026-10-23,
      no tilt or spin on the way out), then closeUp collapses its height on --reflow and removes it on that transitionend,
      with a fixed fallback timer (a design constant, not a measurement); a departing card is kept out of fresh paints and
      re-inserted at its place. Reduced motion (in-app or OS): nothing
      animates and the card goes at once; the stamp's end state is styled to
      show. A held voice decision (CardView.held {seconds, undo}) renders
      .held (amber edge), the 3 s count bar and the kernel-owned text
      "Allowing in N · say “undo”" (the kernel does not report holds yet, so
      app.ts passes none). Droop: a failed card droops once as it lands, a
      rail row droops once when its session flips to failed in this page;
      never a shake. Tests: test/desk.test.ts.
    live-turn: >-
      T-2026-10-21-007 (founder dogfood 2026-10-21, session hsid:v1:01M5E2G1TRBTMST63ZAY9V0W7D seq 4683-4791).
      Turn anchoring (core/store.ts chatItems): turn.sent carries the turn id and turn.result none, and the
      backend answers turns in send order, so a result pairs with the OLDEST open turn.sent (FIFO). A message
      sent while an earlier turn runs WAITS (composer echo, sent voice turn; a refused send stays with it); the
      running turn's output, cards and result are placed before the first waiting message, so a result shows
      under its own turn and never under the next message; the waiting message starts when the earlier result
      lands (or claude replays it); session.exited / orphaned / drained / open settle everything. Nothing
      waiting = plain append. Running state: chatItems({live}) (the page passes isLiveState of the session)
      adds one `working` row (key work:<seq>) under the running turn with a LiveClock {since, progress} from
      the turn start and the latest tool_progress heartbeat (elapsed_time_seconds, tool_name) or
      system.task_started; foldActivity makes that turn's latest activity line live (no "of work" yet), and a
      reply or result closes the segment so the line freezes at the real end (a card between the tool and the
      reply no longer freezes it at the last tool row). core/live-turn.ts (pure): liveSecs / toolSecs /
      liveText ("working… · 2m 6s"; " · running 2m 10s · Bash 1m 33s"), hasLive, LiveTicker (ONE interval
      while the focused transcript has a running turn, cleared when it ends; each tick rewrites only the mounted
      .live-clock spans). ui/app.ts paintTranscript keeps the common key prefix mounted and measured and
      rebuilds only the changed tail (HeightIndex.truncate), so the working row moving down costs no full
      remount. Review H1: in BOTH repaint branches the kept prefix is diffed by rendered signature
      (core/live-turn.ts itemSig: role, text, live, took, said, voice marks; a card's decided state is its
      text) and changedBefore's indices are remounted too, so an activity line frozen by the reply (same key,
      live removed) never keeps a stale .live class or a frozen "running" span; re-review L-4: each such
      remounted index is HeightIndex.invalidate'd (back to the estimate until measured). Review M1: the composer echo
      (Row.turn) is stamped with the turn id session.send returns and pairs with turn.sent{turn} EXACTLY (an
      unstamped echo, its send still in flight, pairs in send order with the first turn.sent no stamp claims);
      a refused or network-failed send marks the echo unsent (Row.unsent): it never waits, never becomes the
      running message, and its reason shows under it, so the next send gets the right clock and order.
      Review M2: open turns are tracked by id (openTurns); turn.result{turn} closes every open turn up to the one
      it names (a queued message Claude Code folded into the running turn settles with it, no working row left
      ticking); a waiting message stamped for a closed turn is dropped, and the next waiting message starts only
      when it is unstamped or its turn is the next open one; a row without turn (older logs) closes the oldest.
      A11y: the working row is role=status, aria-label "Claude is working"; its .live-clock span is
      aria-live=off (the per-second tick is never announced). CSS .trow.role-working
      (spinner, still under reduced motion) and .role-activity.live.
    dogfood-layout-chat: >-
      Dogfood round 2 (2026-10-19). LAYOUT: the shell is a 100dvh flex
      column (header, notices, desk grows, status line); the desk is a
      three-column grid of panes that each scroll inside (sessions list,
      chat viewport, decision pile); under 900px one column, and sessions /
      decisions become drawers behind header toggles with a scrim (no
      horizontal overflow). The grid-row layout it replaces put the desk in
      an auto row once the hidden notices dropped out, so the app sat in
      the top ~290px. CHAT: core/store.ts chatItems turns a session's rows
      into the conversation: the user's message (this page's composer echo,
      else claude's --replay-user-messages line; session.inject / turn.sent
      carry only a hash), assistant text, one tool line per tool_use
      (toolSummary: name + command/path/pattern…), cards inline, the
      turn.result (subtype, cost, tokens) and lifecycle notes; hooks,
      stream_event partials, rate limits, status, control frames, tool
      results and bookkeeping rows are hidden and counted, and "show raw
      events" shows every row. RAW VIEW (founder 2026-10-23 "is there a way
      to know what is being shown here"): turnEventSummary says what each
      claude-code line is (system lines by subtype and identifying fields:
      hooks by hook_event/hook_name, short hook_id and outcome/exit code,
      init by model and cwd; tool results by id, outcome and size; rate
      limits; stream partials; control frames; results with turns, time and
      cost); hook and tool output never enter the summary. Each raw row folds
      (transcript-row variant raw, the activity fold's expanded set, foldRaw
      + rawFoldKey) to its whole row (rowDetail: the line pretty-printed,
      nested {redacted} values kept redacted, withheld/redacted/oversize rows
      have no fold, capped at 20k) in a <pre class="raw-line"> text node that
      scrolls inside itself. A composer echo hides the matching replay so
      the list only grows at the end. STICKINESS: core/follow.ts
      (isAtBottom, Follow) — at the bottom it stays stuck through new rows
      and sends; scrolled up nothing moves it (not even a send), a
      "↓ latest · N new" key jumps back, and scrolling to the bottom by hand
      re-sticks. Founder report 2026-10-23 (it stopped following while he
      spoke): stickiness changes ONLY on the user's own scroll (ScrollIntent:
      a wheel, scroll keys, focus moving into the feed, a pointer or finger
      held on it or its scrollbar); scrollEvent calls any other scroll
      'layout' and leaves it alone. Root cause: WebKit (the Gnomon.app
      wrapper) clamps the feed's scrollTop when the composer shrinks or
      re-measures (fitComposer resets its height to measure) and fires that
      scroll before the ResizeObserver repaint, so it read as the user moving
      up. Mounted rows sit under a ResizeObserver (rowSizes, watched from the
      next frame, dropRow unobserves) so a row that grows by itself repaints;
      .viewport has overflow-anchor: none; an unfold refocuses its line with
      preventScroll. app.ts paints incrementally (no innerHTML, no
      replaceChildren) and anchors the row in view while heights are
      measured. STALE SESSIONS: GuiStore counts daemon.start boots; a new
      boot ends every live session the old kernel did not exit, the boot
      sweep's session.orphaned marks orphans, a session.open in the new
      boot (a resume) makes it live again, session.exited ends it (the old
      reducer matched a `session.exit` kind that does not exist);
      liveCount() feeds the Shuttle's live count. The kernel's
      status.sessions is still the constant {n: 0}, so the log is the
      source of truth. Tests: test/gui.test.ts (chat transcript, stale
      sessions, stickiness, layout CSS); gnomon test/gui-session-e2e.test.ts
      (real kernel: the chat is user/assistant in order, noise hidden) and
      test/gui-browser-darwin.test.ts (headless Chrome: desk ≥ 80% of a
      2000×1030 viewport, no horizontal overflow at 640px).
    description: >-
      #gui (spec §11.1-§11.5, §4.5). #bare-entry (§2.4 rule 8): the fragment
      may carry an optional `cwd` folder hint (base64url UTF-8, ≤ 1024 bytes;
      a malformed one drops the hint, never the launch); core/launch.ts
      cwdHintOf escapes and caps it for display and applyCwdHint opens the
      new-session form, shows it as text in #ns-hint, prefills #ns-cwd only
      when clean and absolute, and never submits — session.open stays on the
      human's click (test/gui.test.ts). Aegis round 1: the hint is applied
      only inside attach() after the launch token verified (never on a failed
      attach or Reconnect); clearCwdHint on cancel, trusted submit and "+ new";
      the prefill rule is the strict L/N/P/S-or-space rule minus Cf and
      default-ignorables, shared with the CLI via
      packages/gnomon/test/fixtures/cwd-hint.v1.json. static/boot.js reads the launch fragment
      (#launch=<token>&k=<spki>) and clears it with history.replaceState
      before any other script, handing it to app.js once. core/launch.ts
      decides the key pin (localStorage holds only the kernel public key;
      a changed fragment key re-pins visibly; Reconnect verifies against the
      pin; none ⇒ refuse); hostSurface() (T-2026-10-18-018 N1, M1.13) is
      'wrapper' only for the frozen non-writable non-configurable
      window.gnomonSurface the #gnomon-wrapper document-start script defines
      (a plain browser cannot produce it under the kernel CSP), and then the
      page sends hello surface wrapper and hides the extension-risk badge
      (display only). core/server-sig.ts verifies hello.serverSig with
      WebCrypto Ed25519 over authServerPreimage and binds serverKeyId; each
      hello carries a fresh clientNonce (getRandomValues, 32 bytes) that the
      result must echo (client-nonce-mismatch) and the signature must cover
      (T-2026-10-18-016); card
      decision keys only for kernel-signed actions that verify. core/client.ts
      is a MINIMAL in-bundle gnomon-rpc:v1 client on gnomon-contracts (hello,
      sig check, auth {launchToken}|{reconnect}, calls, notifications,
      gnomonPost for POST /diag and /blob with X-Gnomon-Token and
      referrerPolicy same-origin; per-call timeout; id:null error frames
      surface as a notice + /diag; a call written and unanswered when the
      socket closes rejects DELIVERY_UNKNOWN{delivery-unknown}, a call after
      the close CLOSED{connection-closed} (B7: one client-local spelling with
      the kernel + TS clients), T-2026-10-19-009 item 6; setup treats
      both as stopped) - swapped for the published #client-ts
      (M1.12) in slice 2. The GUI defines NO sanitizer (Aegis C1): every
      string goes through gnomon-contracts sanitizeDisplayText (display.ts,
      tested with conformance/display.v1.json through the render path, plus
      a fence test); core/render.ts renders the closed kit and kernel cards
      as DOM TEXT NODES only (no innerHTML); a block kit.Button is not a
      decision key and is live only for BLOCK_SAFE_COMMANDS (never diag.send
      or gui.reconnect). Card decision keys only for kernel-signed actions
      whose keyId is the hello's serverKeyId, cached per (cardId,
      contentHash) and cleared when the verify key changes. A re-pin is a
      sticky kernel-owned notice with old/new keyIds and a /diag line.
      core/store.ts reduces log.read rows into sessions by project, per-hsid
      transcripts and the decision stack (order independent, per-project
      filter); core/virtual.ts is the Fenwick-tree virtualized transcript
      with per-width height caches; core/commands.ts the palette, layout
      presets and theme/motion resolution. ui/app.ts wires the page: launch,
      Reconnect, backlog paging + follow subscription, sessions sidebar with
      new session (session.open), composer (session.send), decision stack
      (approve on trusted gestures; an ask-user card with a verified
      `answer` key gets a picker built ONLY from askDetailOf: the card block's
      one {type:'ask-user', detail} node whose detail recomputes (with kind,
      requester, hsid, flags; cardContentHash) to the card's contentHash —
      display text is never parsed; missing/malformed/mismatched => no
      picker (Aegis C1); radio/checkbox per option plus a free-text field
      (aria-label, maxlength = detail.maxAnswerChars), askNote (null-
      prototype answers) builds the
      approve note: plain text for one question, JSON {answers} for several;
      a Bash permission card (TD-2026-10-20-294) splits `always` into
      "Always: this exact command" and one key per prefix choice, taken ONLY
      from prefixOptionsOf (the one {type:'bash-prefix', detail} node whose
      detail recomputes to the contentHash); approveParamsOf turns the
      clicked key's data-scope/data-prefix into approve{scope} (only for
      always; a malformed key sends no scope, so the exact rule); an
      Edit/Write card with a verified {type:'edit-scope'} node (editScopesOf)
      offers "this exact edit", "edits to this file" and "edits in this
      repo" (noted "same as auto-edits for this repo"). On either card the
      scoped choices fold under ONE "Always ▾" key (data-always-fold, no
      decision; Mika 2026-10-23): the row stays Allow · Deny · Always ▾, and
      the unfolded .always-choices group lists each choice as its own
      decision key (accessible name "Always: …") with its note visible
      under it; Esc folds back to the key, and the fold and focus survive a
      stack repaint (per card and zone). The mode chip reads "ask · edits by
      rule" (≤1040px "ask ✓", spoken "edits allowed by rule"; the full words
      in its title) while status.runModes carries editsByRule; ask's menu
      line says edits pass by the rule, and the menu's "stop edits by rule"
      entry sends request.rules.revoke, returning focus to the run mode key
      (TD-2026-10-23-939 follow-up);
      refusals shown verbatim until M1.3
      presence), Shuttle view, the kernel-owned extension-risk badge,
      papercraft day / phosphor night / auto themes and reduced motion.
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, paradigm-8, m1-10]
    tests:
      - test/gui.test.ts
      - test/edit-scope.test.ts
      - test/modes.test.ts
      - test/voice.test.ts
      - test/voice-client.test.ts
      - test/choices.test.ts
      - test/fonts.test.ts
      - test/desk.test.ts
      - test/live-turn.test.ts
      - ../gnomon/test/gui-endpoint.test.ts
      - ../gnomon/test/web-units.test.ts
  gui-setup:
    description: >-
      #gui-setup (spec §11.1, §11.2 rule 11; T-2026-10-19-005 MVP-b) — the
      first-run setup screens over the #setup-endpoint's closed
      gnomon-setup:v1 protocol: a `#setup=<tok>&k=<spki>[&cwd=…]` fragment
      (core/launch.ts parseSetupFragment; never mixed with #launch=) runs
      src/setup instead of the app. route.ts is the state machine (welcome →
      preflight → name → identity 1 of 2 / 2 of 2 → success → handoff; any
      refusal or a closed socket → aborted); hello is verified against the
      fragment setup key with the launch path's verifyServerSig before auth,
      and that key is never stored as the kernel pin. screens.ts renders by
      textContent only; clicks only request steps; the page sends only the
      name and a server-listed gen. digest.ts: the digest is the kernel's
      setup.presence value, shown big and grouped; the copy says the Touch ID
      dialog's last line must BEGIN with `Gnomon Helper: root key signs 1:
      <d12>`, that exactly 2 prompts come, and that cancelling is safe.
    path: src/setup/
    type: module
    gates: ["^setup-token"]
    tags: [gnomon, gui, setup]
    tests:
      - test/setup.test.ts
  gui-relaunch:
    description: >-
      #gui-relaunch page side (T-2026-10-20-001, core/stale.ts). A tab whose
      connection ended outside the self-update path never points to a
      terminal as the only way back and never suggests a reload. It polls its
      own origin (GET /, no credential; 2 s for a minute, then 10 s, ~1 h cap):
      an answer is NOT proof of Gnomon (Aegis L3, a squatter can answer), so it
      says only "something is answering; use the window Gnomon opened", and listens on the same-origin BroadcastChannel
      `gnomon.gui.v1` for a window that attached (`{t:'attached'}`; it asks
      `{t:'who'}`). Exactly those two shapes, no token/key/connId. On
      'attached' it says "Gnomon restarted in a new window" and offers one
      trusted click: Close this tab. The restarted kernel opens its fresh
      window on a NEW OS-chosen port (Aegis H1: no remembered port), so
      across a restart 'attached' arrives only from same-origin tabs. It never rejoins in place: a restarted kernel has a new
      ephemeral key that only a launch fragment delivers (decidePin).
    tags: [gnomon, gui]
    tests:
      - test/stale.test.ts
  gui-stop-speaking:
    description: >-
      #gui Stop speaking (T-2026-10-19-026). A ⏹ "Stop speaking" button beside
      the mic pill (static/index.html #voice-stop), shown only for a human
      connection with the voice app connected (status.voice.clientConnected)
      and status.voice.playback.playing; a trusted click, or Esc when no menu
      or dialog is open and focus is not in the composer, sends ONE log.append
      request.voice.client{op:'stop-speaking'} (narrows: no card, no presence).
      core/voice.ts holds the pure decisions (playbackPlaying,
      stopSpeakingShown, speakPollWanted, escStopsSpeaking); app.ts re-reads
      status every 300 ms (SPEAK_POLL_MS) only while speech plays, plus a 4 s
      watch window after a voice row (playback reports are never logged, so
      the page cannot otherwise see a reply start).
    tags: [voice, gui]
    signals: []
  gui-dictation:
    description: >-
      UNVERIFIED VOICE (Dictate, the G-VOX-06 exception, founder bug
      2026-10-21): a row the kernel stamped draftOnly fills the draft as a
      part marked unverified; the pill note reads "draft · unverified voice ·
      read it, then Enter sends" and the transcript row "in composer ·
      unverified voice"; the send-now key holds such a draft for Enter
      (HOTKEY_UNVERIFIED_NOTE); the word (wordReady and the grace), the piece
      ring (pieceDue) and the countdown (armed) never send it, and a preset
      switch holds it. Aegis privacy: the row is hash-only; app.ts queues live
      voice rows and releaseTurnRows joins the words from
      status.voice.unverified in seq order (a row waits at most
      UNVERIFIED_WAIT_MS, then goes on wordless and never becomes a part).
      sentLabel labels turn.sent origin voice-unverified ("spoken · unverified
      voice · sent by you"); it runs like a typed turn (TD-2026-10-23-939). Mika:
      a mixed draft's note quotes the unverified words (unverifiedQuote,
      cut at UNVERIFIED_QUOTE_MAX with …, full words in the title); an
      unverified row carries no speaker label ("voice · in composer ·
      unverified voice"). A short refused turn (voice-speaker, cause
      too-short) reads "too short to check it's you · say a few more words, or type it" (capture refusalPhrase).
      VOICE SUBMODES (TD-2026-10-21-514, $send-by-word): presets Talk /
      Dictate / Send word / Pieces (src/core/voice-presets.ts; a segmented
      control in the pill menu; Send word and Pieces need the one-time
      liability acknowledgement, recorded per user); the reducer's 'word'
      policy treats a turn that IS the held send word (#send-word-matcher) as
      a command, never appended, acting only on a draft visible ≥ 1 s
      ('painted' via double rAF, page visible, focused, attached; any text
      change resets it); a near miss asks "Did you say …?"; a 1 s grace
      ("Sending… Esc keeps it", draft state word-grace) then
      request.voice.send.claim and the one send path. An ambient attach asks
      for the preset's send ceiling (with liabilityAck once the in-app
      acknowledgement recorded it). Labels: sentLabel(turn.sent) on voice
      messages ("spoken · sent by you / on release / by send word / as a
      piece / by send-now"; the plain origin only since TD-2026-10-23-939,
      which retired the "edits ask first" suffix, the header chip and the
      voice card line with the kernel clamp); teaching the send word INLINE
      under its row in the Voice settings sheet (core/send-word-teach.ts, a
      pure reducer over the kernel's attended trial: pick send / send it /
      over / your own, then "Say <word> once, on its own." and the ONE
      counter "take n of up to 4" from status.voice.sendWordTrial, "I heard
      …", a mishearing kept as a variant, the risk check with "I
      understand" right before save via request.voice.sendword{op:'save'};
      no lead-in, never the product name; Aegis R-1: keeping a mishearing is an
      explicit opt-in, each collected variant an UNTICKED box at save
      ("Saying “x” on its own will also send. You said “w”; I heard “x”.")
      and the save carries every unticked one as dropVariants; only a LISTENING trial makes a turn a take,
      and with the row open nothing heard becomes a draft; the heard text is
      read only from status.voice.sendWordTrial.last);
      a trialTake row is never a transcript line (store voiceItem) and never
      a draft (dictation turnText); Pieces (gap 1500 / cap 8000 ms, hold
      while busy, piece claim, piece ring); Mic key switch, Listening
      (open / toggle) choice sent as the client's capture kind, voice.preset.*
      palette commands, in-app bare `, send-now from the voice app.
      ONE SEND CONTROL (founder report 2026-10-20): the composer's own send
      (Enter / ⌘Enter / [send]) is the only send; the dictation bar has no
      Send of its own. draftState / DRAFT_CONTROLS map the draft's state to
      its controls: idle (none), ambient (no hold: nothing counts down),
      ptt-countdown (ring + [Hold]), ptt-held ([Resume]), ptt-manual (auto-send
      off: no hold). A new dictation mode adds a state and a row. The composer
      is one container: the form carries the border and, while the textarea
      has keyboard focus, the focus ring (:has); the textarea draws none.
      #gui-dictation (TD-2026-10-20-262, T-2026-10-19-026) — voice dictation
      into the composer. core/dictation.ts is a PURE reducer: a live
      voice.turn.user row with the kernel-stamped `forwardable: true`,
      non-empty text, no `intercepted`/refusal, for the attached session and
      past the start seq (no backlog; each seq once) appends to the draft with
      one space. One countdown ring runs over the per-machine delay
      (localStorage gnomon.dictation.delayMs: 3/5/8/15 s/off, default 5 s;
      pill menu picks and voice.delay.* palette commands) while the draft is
      unheld, the voice app idle (status.voice.dictation.activity), the
      session not streaming, and the attached session is the GUI's focused
      one (else the pill says "draft waiting"); new speech, transcription, a
      new turn or streaming resets it to the full delay. Hold: [Hold]/[Resume],
      the voice app's ⌃⌥H (status.voice.dictation.holdToggles, by parity),
      typing in or clicking into a draft. The composer send (Enter/⌘Enter/[send]) sends now. The
      send is session.send{hsid, content: one part per turn | the edit as ONE
      part, source: voice}. The #gui store reads turn.sent voiceTurnSeqs (and
      the older voiceTurnSeq), shows 🎙 for voice and 🎙✎ for voice-edited,
      and a forwardable unsent turn as "in composer". Only a human-class
      connection (canAttach) gets these controls; a voice connection never.
      Aegis conditions: hold records who set it (gui | voice | detached; a
      voice toggle never clears a GUI-set or detached hold); no live
      attachment for the draft's session ⇒ held 'detached', never
      auto-sent; an edit while sending keeps hold and the edit; turn text is
      sanitized by the contracts sanitizeDisplayText (sent as the voice app's
      exact words only when sanitizing changed nothing); the holdToggles
      baseline resets per voice connection (connEpoch, else
      client.restarts); edited drafts echo as typed messages.
      TD-2026-10-20-125 (founder ruling): ambient speech NEVER auto-sends. A
      part whose turn's mode is not exactly 'ptt' (missing included) marks
      the draft ambient (ambientDraft); an ambient draft never arms the ring
      and only the composer send (Enter/⌘Enter/[send]) sends it (note "draft · Enter sends
      (ambient never auto-sends)"). PTT drafts keep the countdown; the delay
      picks say push-to-talk.
      AT THE CARET (founder report 2026-10-23): turnRow carries the
      composer's caret or selection (`at`, app.ts composerCaret: the focused
      selection, else the last caret collapsed so a selection is never
      replaced unseen, else the end; only while the composer shows this
      draft). The plain end of an unedited draft keeps the in-order append
      (plainAppend), so an unedited send is still one part per turn. Anywhere
      else placeWords splices the words in (one space, never two; a capital
      at a sentence start, a plainly capitalised first word lowered
      mid-sentence, never "I" or an acronym; no full stop before the sentence
      goes on) and the draft becomes edited and held: it sends as ONE part
      (source voice; the kernel matches parts in order, so out-of-order parts
      must never go as parts), never as a piece, and the voice send key holds
      it for Enter. The part keeps its unverified / inherited / ambient marks.
      `caret` is where app.ts puts the composer's caret after the turn
      (setSelectionRange, never taking the focus) so speech flows on.
    path: src/core/dictation.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, voice, dictation]
    tests:
      - test/dictation.test.ts
      - test/dictation-caret.test.ts
  gui-preview:
    description: >-
      #gui-preview (DEV ONLY; never in the kernel-served bundle) - the GUI
      fixture preview for designers and agents. scripts/preview.mjs serves
      the REAL static/index.html, boot.js and styles.css on 127.0.0.1 only
      (default port 8790, loopback Host check) with an app.js bundled from
      src/preview/main.ts: the real ui/app.ts and core run over a fake
      kernel Transport (src/preview/fake-kernel.ts) that answers hello with a
      real Ed25519 serverSig from a per-page throwaway WebCrypto key, auth,
      status, log.read (backlog + follow), approve (emits approval.decide),
      log.append and session.send (no effect), and refuses session.open.
      Card actions are signed with the same key, so the real GUI verifies
      and renders the decision keys. Fixtures (src/preview/fixtures.ts:
      contracts LogRow chains of registered kinds plus the status result;
      desk, empty, voice-armed, voice-crashed, stack-heavy, workshop, spoken,
      choices) are
      chosen by URL ?fixture=&theme=day|night&motion=on|off[&surface=browser];
      src/preview/env.ts stubs only the colour-scheme and reduced-motion
      media queries and the wrapper surface marker. The workshop fixture runs
      the real Workshop mod model (packages/gnomon-mods/workshop/model.mjs)
      over the feed projection and draws it with renderBlock. / lists every
      fixture x theme; --fixture-list prints the URLs.
      scripts/preview-shots.mjs writes <fixture>-<theme>.png at 1440x900 with
      Playwright or Puppeteer when one is already installed (none is added),
      or an installed Chrome with --chrome; otherwise it skips.
      Fixture paradigm-context (#paradigm-context-mod): status.mods.views
      lists the sidebar sheet; the fake kernel answers mod.view like the
      host (the GUI {focus:{hsid}} joined to a fixture K1 slice by hsid,
      other keys ignored) through the REAL mod model
      (src/preview/paradigm-context.ts), drawn by the real mod-panel path.
    path: src/preview/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, dev-tool, preview]
    tests:
      - test/preview.test.ts
  gui-voice-capture:
    description: >-
      TD-2026-10-23-496: under Send word the word sends the whole draft,
      unchecked parts included (wordReady no longer blocks on them, a switch
      to Send word no longer holds the draft); the note reads "draft · some
      words not checked as you · say '<word>' or press Enter"; the risk
      sentence says the word sends everything, even unchecked words, and
      that anyone near the mic can send with it. Send-now and pieces still
      hold an unverified draft for Enter.
      Aegis H-1 (2026-10-23): a turn that inherited its speaker
      (speakerBasis 'continuity') is a draft part marked inherited: the row
      reads "in composer · not checked as you", the draft note "draft ·
      [“words”] not checked as you" (information: no clamp), a piece needs a part
      checked as the human; the refusal causes inherited-only / inherited
      read in plain words. A short unverified push-to-talk turn (draftOnly)
      stops the Talk countdown. The input picker opens, renews (10 s) and
      closes the mic meter (request.voice.client{op:'mic-meter'}).
      2026-10-23: a refused voice send reads in plain words
      (voiceRefusalText: "✕ not sent by voice · Gnomon couldn't confirm it
      was you for part of this draft" + next: press Enter to send it · or
      re-teach your voice on this mic), never the code, symbol or rule id.
      Voice drops fix (2026-10-20): a drop names its reason in words
      (dropLabelOf, refusalPhrase) and stays on the pill until the next capture
      or a dismiss (captureDismiss on opening the voice menu); the store renders
      kernel-refused hash-only voice.turn.user rows (refusedReason,
      refusedCause) as voice-refused.
      #gui-voice-capture (T-2026-10-20-005 A1, TD-2026-10-20-086 V3/V4) — live
      capture feedback. core/capture.ts is PURE: captureStatusOf is the one
      adapter over status.voice.capture{state, segId, reason?, level?, at}
      (the voice app's per-segment state, relayed by the kernel with a 5 s
      TTL); captureStep/captureDisplayOf give the pill words: idle keeps
      "Listening" / "Hold … to talk" (meter still), hearing "Hearing you…"
      (pulsing, the meter is the REAL level), transcribing "Catching that…",
      captured "Got it" (1.2 s flash), dropped the reason only for 2.5 s
      (no words, no count). capturePollMs is the V3 cadence (no push relay):
      ~1 s at rest, 175 ms while hearing or transcribing, null when off,
      detached, the voice app gone or disconnected; app.ts syncClientPoll
      runs the one attached poll at that cadence (single flight,
      pollStatusOnce) and stopStatusPolls clears every status poll and the
      flash timer on disconnect (Aegis L2 of 862ef85a). The composer ghost
      line "…" is its own element (#composer-ghost, never the textarea); the
      polite caption (#voice-caption) changes on a state change only. The
      decorative meter animation and row kick are gone, and the dead
      voice.turn.partial path is removed. B1 live words (T-2026-10-20-005,
      V1/V2): captureStatusOf reads capture.text{committed, tail} (hearing /
      transcribing only; ghostTextOf: strings only, whitespace collapsed,
      capped at GHOST_TEXT_MAX keeping the newest words), which the kernel
      projects to the human gui credential only; app.ts paintGhost puts the
      committed words solid (.ghost-committed) and the tail dim
      (.ghost-tail) as text nodes into #composer-ghost (never the textarea,
      so a send can never carry non-final words), "…" with no words, and
      clears on captured / dropped / idle. Reduced motion: the global rule
      makes the tail fade instant. AT THE CARET (founder report 2026-10-23):
      #composer-ghost is now an aria-hidden mirror laid over the textarea
      (placeGhost: same box, font and wrapping; scrolled with it) that draws
      the composer text with the live words where the turn will land
      (placeWords, the reducer's rule, at composerCaret); the textarea's own
      text is transparent while it shows (.ghosting, caret kept) and still
      never holds a live word. Committed words carry a dotted --sec
      underline; fitComposer grows the composer to fit them.
      Aegis follow-ups: a capture from a status received more than
      CAPTURE_STALE_MS (5 s) ago is never shown (freshCapture, page clock);
      a captured the kernel marks kernel:'unconfirmed' reads "Heard, not
      confirmed", never "Got it".
    path: src/core/capture.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, voice, capture]
    flows: [$voice-turn]
    tests:
      - test/capture.test.ts
  gui-mods-panel:
    description: >-
      The Mods panel (founder dogfood 2026-10-21: "Install Workshop does
      nothing; no way to see which mods are on"). core/mods.ts (PURE):
      modsViewOf(status, stack cards) gives installed / available / pending;
      request builders for request.mod.install|link|pause|start|uninstall|
      config; folderPathError; configRequest (only manifest-declared fields,
      secrets refused). ui/mods-panel.ts: the sheet (no header key since board header-5b: Gnomon menu, ⌘K, Workshop; created in
      code, no index.html change), palette mods.open, Esc closes, trusted
      presses only, every key busy then a result in words (refusals as
      alerts), "decide in the stack" focuses the card. Install Workshop
      (core/mod-panels.ts workshopInstallKey, ui/mod-panels-mount.ts
      installWorkshop) now sends request.mod.install or opens the panel;
      it was a disabled constant with the command in title= only.
    tags: [gui, mods]
    signals: []
    tests:
      - test/mods.test.ts
      - test/workshop.test.ts

  gui-loops:
    description: >-
      LP8, the GUI Loops view (docs/specs/gnomon-loops.md §6; Atelier
      2026-10-22-gnomon-loops-ui, design-system loops-word, loops-leaf,
      loop-row, loop-list, loop-detail, budget-field, loop-graph, run-trace,
      loop-trust-unfolded, loop-diff, alert, trust-slip, toast loop-done).
      core/loops.ts (PURE) reads the human class's status.loops (registry
      list with each loop's drawable shape and authoredBy, the runner's
      running set and run ledger, effective autonomy with capReason, the
      uptime hold) into the header loops word, the leaf meta, keep-alive
      line and edge tab, the needs-you-pinned project-grouped two-line
      rows, detail keys that name their cost, budget keys (tighter /
      looser), the run trace and run paths, stack alerts (fail, stop,
      kernel pause), the waiting-for-trust slip, loop-done toasts from live
      loop.run.ended{goal}, loop.landed and loop.notified rows, and the
      unfolded trust card's sections. core/loop-graph.ts (PURE) lays the
      graph out left to right when it fits, else top to bottom, with
      collapsed labels (any / else), merged buses, boxes sized to their
      type line, marks for verdicts; fit plus zoom inside the frame.
      ui/loops-view.ts is the DOM (the centre leaf, Esc folds it to the
      edge tab; Read unfolds a loop-trust card over the centre). Requests
      are log.append of request.loop.* on a trusted press; Pause all is
      request.loop.pause{all:true} (palette loops.pause-all, the leaf head,
      the wordmark menu). Apply · tighter sends request.loop.budget (narrowing only, the kernel's loop.budget.tightened row); a looser cap is disabled as Loosen · needs trust. Loop cards are identified from the card:v1 the broker sends (the root-rows node, the kernel's loop.notified row, the kernel line), never a top-level detail.
    tags: [gui, loops]
    signals: []
    tests:
      - test/loops-view.test.ts
      - test/loop-cards.test.ts
      - test/desk.test.ts

  gui-turn-steps:
    description: >-
      Founder 2026-10-23 ("with gnomon seeing what the stop hooks are doing
      … in that little chip label and then after the result of it"; then
      "just right there where that 'working label' area is just a little
      bit of labeling on what is being called … clicking on it to expand
      out to see what is being done"). core/turn-steps.ts (PURE):
      StepTracker folds the running turn's full turn.event lines (main
      chain only) into steps: thinking / writing (content blocks), a tool
      call (calling <Tool>, then toolSummary's '<Tool> · <target>' until its
      tool_result: ok | error), a hook (hook_started to hook_response under
      #claude-adapter's --include-hook-events: '<Event> hook[ · matcher]',
      outcome ok | blocked (exit 2 or stdout JSON decision block, the
      reason's first line) | timed out (cancelled) | failed (exit N); Claude's
      synthetic 'Stop hook feedback' line names a blocking hook's command
      by its script basename), a status (compacting). now() is the working
      key's words and clock start (running hooks first, else the latest open
      step, else 'finishing' after the main-chain end_turn, else working…);
      a running hook carries `under` (what the key named before it), and
      live-turn.ts workNow shows it until the hook has run HOOK_DWELL_MS
      (1 s), so a fast PreToolUse hook never flicks the key;
      summary() is the turn's one hook-result line (notable hook groups:
      not ok, or 2 s or more; failed tool calls; warn only when a hook
      blocked, failed or timed out), placed by store.ts chatItems before the
      turn's result line. withStepFolds attaches rowDetail (the raw fold's
      redaction) to unfolded steps. store.ts lineItems never shows a
      synthetic user line as the human's (hook feedback folds into the
      hook-result line, other synthetic lines are a quiet system line).
      ui/app.ts workingEl: the working row is a key (role=button,
      aria-expanded, Enter / Space / click; data-act steps:<key>; its full
      words in title) whose words ellipsize and whose clock never does
      (live-turn.ts workParts); it unfolds an ol.steps (a labelled list,
      clocks aria-hidden, 24px rows, max 40vh, scrolls inside itself, keeps
      its scroll across remounts); each step's words ellipsize before its
      time and outcome (stepParts); a finished step folds to its lines. The
      row is no live region (it remounts per step): sayWork writes the
      persistent #turn-say status ("Claude is waiting on a Stop hook") once
      what the turn does has held 2 s. The ticker rewrites the key's words
      and clocks; itemSig repaints on a step change, never per tick.
      Preview fixtures turn-hook, turn-hooks, turn-steps replay the 2026-10-23
      hook probes' lines. Design: .atelier/systems/gnomon transcript-row
      variants working, step-list, hook-result (reviewed: atelier-mika
      2026-10-23, amended), claude-note (Aegis M1).
      Aegis review 2026-10-23: M1 a synthetic user line that is not
      "<event>[:matcher] hook feedback:" is role claude-note ("Claude ·
      <text>"), never 'system' (the kernel's notes); L1 Claude's feedback
      names a blocked hook only when that step's own reason first line is
      the same text (no reason, no name); M2 StepTracker.push takes the
      kernel's turn.event.hook facts (kernel principal only) so a line
      stored by hash still opens and ends its step, and hookOutcome takes
      the outcome from them (a {bytes, sha256} field has no reason text).
      Mika: a hook Claude cancelled reads "timed out" unless the turn was
      interrupted ("[Request interrupted by user]" within 2 s after it,
      measured on claude 2.1.309): then "cancelled", quiet (no warn).
    tags: [gui, transcript, hooks]
    signals: []
    tests:
      - test/turn-steps.test.ts
      - test/live-turn.test.ts

  gui-offer-slip:
    description: >-
      The Desk's margin slip (TD-2026-10-20-812 O1, Luna's comp
      .atelier/sessions/2026-10-20-gnomon-mod-invitations refs/flow.html).
      core/offers.ts (PURE): foldOffers folds ONLY the kernel's offer.shown /
      offer.decided / offer.kept rows of one conversation (principal
      p:<ns>/kernel, payload hsid = the conversation, offer:<ULID>, a
      turn:<hsid>/<n> replyTurnId, single-line question <= 240 code points),
      never reply text; slipViews mounts each slip under the last assistant
      item before its offer.shown row and makes only the newest undecided slip
      live, only while its reply is the latest and no human message follows;
      openStep is the two-step open (A5: first trusted click/Enter arms and
      shows "takes: <manifest contextIn> · ↵ to open", the second sends);
      decideRequest = log.append{kind:request.offer.decide,
      payload:{offerId, decision}}; offer.decided closes the slip, not-now
      quiets that mod for the rest of the conversation (L4), stop-here
      quiets all; voiceOfferIntent: a heard "not now" dismisses (one request
      per offer, live rows only), a heard "open" only shows "click or ↵ to
      open" (L1). Re-review M-2: a kernel offer.retired{why:'continued'}
      closes an undecided slip (never live, no voice dismissal) and leaves
      the trace "retired · the reply continued · mod:<name>". Aegis fixes: M1 openStep refuses key repeats and
      multi-clicks, waits OFFER_ARM_GAP_MS (400) after the arm, and drops an
      arm after OFFER_ARM_TTL_MS (15 s); M2 only a forwardable,
      non-intercepted push-to-talk row (pttDismissable) dismisses, only the
      slip live when it arrived, only rows after offerLiveSince; ambient
      speech shows "click not now to dismiss"; M3 "takes:" comes from the
      row's kernel-copied contextIn (contracts CONTEXT_SOURCES labelled by
      CONTEXT_SOURCE_LABELS, unknown tokens shown as unknown, +N more past
      8, missing = "unknown (not reported by the kernel)"); L1
      devArmOfferOnce is dead code in the served bundle (__GNOMON_PREVIEW__
      define false + minifySyntax in build.mjs). The offer kinds, patterns,
      CONTEXT_SOURCES and the isOfferTitle / isOfferQuestion text rules are
      imported from @a-company/gnomon-contracts. stripOfferBlocks (called by
      store.ts chatItems) hides a reply's trailing ```offer block (contracts
      offerBlockOf body) ONLY when a valid kernel offer.shown row anchors to
      that reply and the block names the same mod and kind; otherwise the
      reply text shows as-is (model text alone never hides anything).
      ui/offer-slip.ts:
      renderOfferSlip (dashed, soft shadow, never .key / data-decision; tab =
      glyph + offer · mod:<name>, no per-mod hue, L2; the question a text
      node) and wireOfferSlips (trusted click / Enter only). ui/app.ts mounts
      the slips in itemEl and syncs them in paintTranscript; styles.css
      .slip* (-0.7deg by day via --slip-tilt, flat at night, a slide-in of up to 320ms,
      instant under reduced motion). Preview fixtures offer-slip,
      offer-armed (devArmOfferOnce, DEV ONLY), offer-muted; the fake kernel
      answers request.offer.decide with offer.decided. Tests:
      test/offers.test.ts.
    signals: []
  gui-table-talk:
    description: >-
      #gui-table-talk (TD-2026-10-20-294) — a reply's first speak fenced block
      (store.ts splitSpeak, mirroring the kernel projector) shows as a
      highlighted "said aloud" line at the top of the reply and is removed
      from the body; a reply without one (heuristic) gets no highlight. Lines
      that start with a bold label, in whatever scheme the agent chose
      (letters, numbers, short names), render as .reply-part lines (replyParts: a quiet left rule and a bold
      label; board gnomon-chip renamed them from .chip, they were never chips).
      Aegis L3: when the kernel's speakable row (principal p:<ns>/kernel) for
      that reply exists, the line is its text (from block, "said aloud";
      heuristic shows none); otherwise the GUI's own parse ("spoken part").
      Aegis M1: a replayed user message always keeps content[0]; a later text
      block is hidden only when its sha256 is the kernel guidance hash
      (TABLE_TALK_GUIDANCE_HASH, pinned to the kernel's) or the turn.sent
      guidanceHash; a human-typed <gnomon-voice> stays visible.
      One spoken-aloud marker per reply (founder bug 2026-10-20): pipelined
      TTS logs one playback voice.turn.agent per sentence; chatItems
      (spokenFold/spokenText) opens ONE 🔊 marker at the kernel's speakable
      row (or the first playback row on an older kernel) and folds every
      later playback row and voice.bargein into it until the next assistant
      reply: "🔊 spoken aloud · 5s", "· stopped" when any chunk was cut off
      (interrupted, shorter than planned, or a barge-in); a barge-in with no
      marker stays the lone "🔊 interrupted". app.ts paintTranscript
      repaints a mounted row whose text changed in place. Preview fixture
      `spoken`.
      Clickable reply options (core/choices.ts, PURE): replyChoices finds
      2..6 option lines keyed A..F or 1..6 in order (separator space ) . :,
      optional bold) at the END of a reply that asks a question (in the text
      above or the said-aloud line); labels go through the contracts
      sanitizer and are at most 120 chars, else no chips. liveChoiceKey: only
      the last assistant item of the focused session, while the human has
      not written after it; older replies render the chips disabled. Chips
      are dashed buttons (.choice, ink keycap by day, [A] at night) with
      data-choice / data-choice-item, never the key class or data-decision.
      pickChoice: trusted gesture only; the sent text is rebuilt from the
      parsed reply (`A — <label>`), put into the composer and sent via the
      composer form's requestSubmit (the typed-message path); a draft
      (typed or dictated) is kept and the option appended, nothing sent.
      Keys: letter/number pick inside the live group when the composer is
      empty, arrows move, Enter activates. Voice picking is out of scope.
      Preview fixture `choices`. Tests: test/choices.test.ts.
      Aegis review folded in: M1 a letter/number key only moves focus to its
      chip (Enter/Space confirms); a label over 60 chars, with a backtick or
      shell-like text needs a confirming second click/Enter (.choice.armed,
      "again to send"). M2 any option the contracts sanitizer flags ⇒ no
      chips. L1 night chips show a plain underlined letter, no [ ] brackets.
      L2 send() returns whether the kernel took the message; a chip is marked
      picked only then, and the composer clears only when the message went
      out (never on an early return). L3 onChoice recomputes liveness from
      currentItems(). L4 more than two combining marks on a base ⇒ no chips.
    path: src/core/store.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, voice, table-talk]
    tests:
      - test/table-talk.test.ts
  gui-wordmark-menu:
    description: >-
      #gui-wordmark-menu (board header-5b, Atelier 2026-10-21-gnomon-voice
      refs/header-5b.html option C; design-system gnomon.voice.header) - the
      header row is four things: the wordmark menu "Gnomon ▾", the ⌘K palette
      field, quiet kernel status (#conn link dot, word only when not
      connected; #risk outlined amber chip, "browser · extension risk" wide
      and "browser · risk" below 1040px (Aegis: the narrow chip still says
      risk), full text in title and sr-only, shown from boot on the browser
      surface before any attach and hidden only in the wrapper) and the
      kernel-owned voice pill. Every control
      28px, nowrap; the row never wraps (palette words, then the pill fact,
      truncate). PURE core/header.ts: HEADER_ITEMS, appMenuModel (Layout
      presets, "Panes and Workshop…" opening pane toggles + Workshop
      placement in place, Day/Night/Auto radios, Mods…, Voice settings…,
      Settings… ⌘,, who line), APP_MENU_RUNS (existing GUI commands only),
      triggerKey / menuKey (Enter/Space are the click, ↓/↑ open on first /
      last, arrows/Home/End move, Esc closes and focus returns, Tab closes),
      linkView, whoLine. The theme switch, ⚙, Mods and ⊞ Layout header keys,
      the separate Start voice key and the loose voice note are gone: while
      the voice app can't run the pill IS the action (voice-client.ts
      pillActionOf: "Start voice · app not running", aria-label says what a
      click does); attached, the action is the ladder's first row; a draft
      waiting elsewhere is the pill's fact; the idle auto-off is the 6 s
      toast in ladder words. Palette: menu.gnomon "Gnomon menu: …" (not
      block-safe). Preview fixture app-menu.
    path: src/core/header.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, header]
    tests:
      - test/header.test.ts
  gui-voice-ladder:
    description: >-
      #gui-voice-ladder (Atelier 2026-10-21-gnomon-voice, direction.html;
      design-system gnomon.voice.model + pill) - voice is ONE choice, a trust
      ladder Off / Talk / Dictate / Send word / Pieces mapped onto the voice
      state x send preset (Off = voice.session.end, Talk = ptt x countdown,
      Dictate = open/toggle x key, Send word = word, Pieces = pieces). PURE
      core/voice-ladder.ts: rungOf (the kernel's status.voice.send wins over
      the page's preset), ladderEntries (one line each, cost tags), chooseRung
      (a not-ready rung names the Voice settings section that readies it),
      voicePillOf (the kernel-owned header pill: mic dot filled + ring when
      open, rung name, ONE live fact: hold ⌃⌥Space / listening / say “word” /
      mic off · ⌃` / heard Ns ago; vermilion "not sent · why"; no clamp
      fact or edge since TD-2026-10-23-939), sheetRows.
      The popover (role menu, rungs menuitemradio, arrows/Home/End, Esc back
      to the pill) holds the ladder only plus a foot line (mic key · listen)
      and "voice settings…"; the old Off/Push-to-talk/Ambient list, delay
      buttons and Send preset buttons are gone. Luna finish-review: Pieces
      reads "set up · Touch ID" while not ready; when the focused session is
      not the attached one the ladder (and its aria name) says "applies to
      <B> · voice is on <A>" (ladderTargetLine / ladderAria); a crash's fact is
      just "voice crashed", its cause in the title and aria name
      (crashCauseOf); the risk row says when it was acknowledged; the mic dot
      and meter are --ink (board gnomon-status-colour retired --live and --stamp); the pill
      meter shows only while capture is `hearing` (capture.ts meterShownOf);
      night selected segments are [bracketed] with the glow; the tall-view
      key has a pressed state. Copy retirement (T-2026-10-21-016): the
      palette's voice.off / voice.ptt / voice.ambient are gone; the ladder's
      voice.preset.off|talk|dictate|send-word|pieces are the only voice rung
      commands (rungOfPresetCommand), the Talk hotkey rides voice.preset.talk,
      and every user-facing string speaks the rungs (rungNameOf: Off, Talk,
      Dictate, Send word, Pieces; "open mic" for the shared ambient state),
      never "Ambient" / "push-to-talk"; the store's spoken markers ("spoken
      aloud", "interrupted") and the card voice tag ("voice · reversible",
      "voice · gate") are words, no emoji (gnomon cli-voice); the Gnomon
      menu's theme row is Day / Night / Auto without glyphs. Wire values and
      identifiers ('ambient', 'ptt', 'conversation', voice-ambient) are
      unchanged. test/copy-vocabulary.test.ts walks every string literal in
      core/ for the retired words and the emoji set.
    path: src/core/voice-ladder.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, voice]
    tests:
      - test/voice-ladder.test.ts
      - test/voice.test.ts
      - test/copy-vocabulary.test.ts
  gui-voice-settings:
    description: >-
      2026-10-23 (founder request): an input row first (the mic in use:
      name, transport, rate, echo cancelling, system default or chosen; warn
      when the chosen mic is missing or the mic stopped) whose flow is the
      picker (core/voice-ladder.ts inputRow / inputChoices: system default,
      every input, a missing choice kept; the folder field's choice rows
      .ff-row.plain with "in use", one Tab stop, arrows move focus and
      Enter or Space chooses; a role=meter level from status.voice.mic.level,
      re-read every INPUT_METER_POLL_MS while open) and
      request.voice.client{op:'select-input'}. The pill's title names the mic
      (micTitleLine); a chosen mic that is not connected appends "· chosen mic
      missing", a mic fault "· mic stopped: <short cause>"
      (micFaultFact; the whole sentence in the title, the aria name and the
      ladder's Restart row; the dot hollow). voiceRefusalText applies on the
      send path only (unsentEcho), not to every voice-* refusal.
      #gui-voice-settings (Atelier 2026-10-21, setup-home.html + teach.html) -
      the Voice settings sheet, a right-side drawer on the sheet component
      (role dialog, Esc closes, focus returns): your voice (inline enrolment:
      name + consent, Touch ID, "phrase N of 3" with the phrase and a REAL
      level meter), send word (inline teaching over request.voice.sendword
      start{trial} / save / clear{trial}), keys (talk ⌃⌥Space, mic ⌃` via
      the existing mic-key op with the bare ` opt-in warning, send now
      ⌃⌥Return), listen (always / mic key), timing (Talk auto-send 3/5/8/15/off
      as a segmented control; pieces gap shown), risk (acknowledged or not; a
      waiting Pieces turns on from here). ui/voice-settings.ts builds with
      render.ts h() and routes every trusted press through one act callback;
      the old sendword / ack / enrol dialogs are removed. The trial never
      outlives the row or the sheet. The risk check is the render's sentence
      naming the word (voice-presets riskSentence; Pieces names the pause)
      with the ACK_TEXT box; once this user acknowledged it shows
      "acknowledged · <date>" (recordAck keeps the date, ackedAt) instead of a
      pre-ticked box. The recommended send words skip the common-word
      warning. While open, Tab is trapped inside the aria-modal drawer
      (trapNext) and focus returns on close.
    path: src/ui/voice-settings.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, voice, settings]
    tests:
      - test/voice-ladder.test.ts
      - test/voice-client.test.ts
  gui-chip:
    description: >-
      #gui-chip (board gnomon-chip, design-system rule chip-is-not-a-key,
      migration batch chips-and-small-keys) - a chip is a status label nobody
      clicks: <span class="chip">, 18px, 10.5, the faint --rule edge, radius 3
      by day and square at night; tones plain (card voice tag, mod tier), ink
      (.chip.ink and the mod-kit `chip` tone .tone-chip) and warn (.chip.warn:
      card flags, mod pending, dev). The gate handle in the
      voice tag keeps its warn fill at radius 3. It replaces .badge,
      .card-voice's own edge and .tone-chip's own look (the clamp pill is gone with the clamp, TD-2026-10-23-939). Never
      a <button>, never focusable. Anything clickable is a key: every
      .key.quiet is at least 24 x 24 (⋯, ⤢, Hold, Stop speaking, close), and
      ✎ rename, the run mode ▾ and the stack filter are 24px quiet keys with
      the --key-edge at 11.5 (the chat header row grows 6px); all keep the
      .key:focus-visible ring.
    path: static/styles.css
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, design-system, chip]
    tests:
      - test/desk.test.ts
  gui-type:
    description: >-
      #gui-type (board gnomon-type-scale, choice four-steps; design-system
      foundations.type; migration batch type) - four type steps as tokens in
      static/styles.css :root: --fs-label 10.5 (caps labels, card heads,
      chips, timestamps, notes, the status line, Workshop words, kbd hints,
      the .choice-k key),
      --fs-control 11.5 (keys incl. .key.quiet, menu items,
      session rows, field text, toasts, tool and result lines, the pill),
      --fs-reading 13.5 (body, replies, reply choices, card titles, section
      heads, night titles, the heard phrase at 600) and --fs-title 17
      (wordmark, sheet and pane titles incl. the stack head, chat, empty and
      setup titles, the setup digest); at night the stack, settings and
      setup titles are 13.5, carried by typeface and case. A setup card's title is
      13.5 at 600. Every font-size uses one; no literal
      remains, and none is set inline from TS. Hierarchy beyond size is
      weight, case and face (card title and settings section head at 600).
      The Workshop 76px column's text is 10.5: titles, texts, labels and the
      absent note wrap (overflow-wrap anywhere), a cap question truncates
      with … at 64px and keeps its full text in title= and aria-label; the
      host and slot drop their cap and padding inside the column. The setup
      digest is 17, weight 600, .08em, one unbroken line of groups of four,
      in var(--mono). Sheet titles (Settings, Voice settings, Mods) are
      <h2 class=title> and their section heads <h3 class="title
      settings-h"> (render.ts h() allows h2/h3), same look as before.
      gnomon-wrapper/static/status.css carries --fs-reading and --fs-title
      for its standalone page, plus copied ground/ink/fail and --mono.
    path: static/styles.css
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, design-system, type]
    tests:
      - test/desk.test.ts
  gui-space-radius:
    description: >-
      #gui-space-radius (board gnomon-spacing, choice 2px-grid; design-system
      foundations.space and foundations.radius; migration batches spacing
      and radius) - every padding, margin and gap in static/styles.css is an
      even number of pixels (no odd px, no rem; .sr-only keeps its -1px clip).
      A key is padding 4px 10px with an 18px line, 28px tall; quiet keys
      2px 8px at min 24. Radius is var(--radius) 3 (keys, fields, cards,
      sheets, menus, chips, toasts, code, swatches), var(--radius-pill) 999
      only for the voice pill, reply choices, the slip's open key and their
      kbd pills, 0 at night where the system squares them, and 50% for dots.
      gnomon-wrapper/static/status.css declares its own --radius 3.
    path: static/styles.css
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, design-system, spacing, radius]
    tests:
      - test/desk.test.ts
  gui-toast:
    description: >-
      #gui-toast (board gnomon-notices, choice band-for-alerts; design-system
      component toast, zone toasts, rule notices-by-kind; migration batch
      notices-and-toasts) - every notice that is not a kernel alert, in one
      style and one place: the #toasts region, a zero-height anchor that is
      the first child of the chat column's .feed (founder's pick, option A of
      Luna's gnomon-toast-placement reference): right-aligned at the chat
      column's right edge under the chat header row, over the conversation,
      never over the chat header's keys or any stack key. With a sheet open
      it lifts above the scrim (z 45) to the window's top right, left of the
      Voice settings drawer; if the desk is removed it moves to the shell
      (.toast-anchor.lifted). One width, min(44ch + 26px, the column). A
      clamped text opens on hover or focus (it is focusable) and a fail is
      never clamped; announcements are appended to the live regions, so two
      quick toasts are both read. A key focuses only its own card
      (ui/card-focus.ts cardIn: the exact cardId, never another gate card);
      when it has not arrived a warn names it (upgrade, grant, re-pin, voice,
      Touch ID card) and clears when it does. Every card focus (focusCard,
      focusCardGroup) first closes the modal New session sheet
      (ui/card-focus.ts uncoverStack): a focus behind an aria-modal sheet
      landed nowhere (founder field test 2026-10-23).
      Known gap: at 1024 a 720px sheet leaves no room, so a toast can cover
      the sheet's close key (tracked separately).
      The band keeps #repin and #voice-dev only. core/toasts.ts (PURE) holds
      the policy: kinds info / warn / fail with the left edge ink / amber /
      vermilion; info leaves after 6 s and warn after 10 s, both paused while
      hovered or focused; fail and persistent never leave by themselves;
      kind is never hue alone: fail and warn carry a caps word in ink
      ("failed", "warning", "asks first") and warn's edge is dashed;
      announcements go through two live regions in index.html (#toast-say
      polite, #toast-alert assertive for fail), the toasts are not live; at
      most three, newest on top and always shown, an older info then warn
      leaves for room, a fail or persistent one waits hidden; a refusal's next: line stays visible while the main
      text clamps to 4 lines at 44ch (the rest in title=). ui/toasts.ts is
      the DOM (text nodes only): an optional single key (Restart now, Make it
      standing, Re-pin) that focuses a card or makes a request and never
      decides a card; a 24px close key on fail and persistent toasts; Esc in
      a toast closes it and the page's Esc closes the newest fail. Focus: a
      new toast is inserted at the top and nothing moves; a focused toast
      that leaves returns focus where it was before, never to another key.
      Its callers: app.ts notice(msg, kind, {held, key, source}) over
      noticeChannel (GUI outcomes; a new one replaces the last unless that
      was a fail; a fail with a source clears when that source succeeds; an
      asks-first step is a held warn; a re-pin "not arrived yet" warn clears
      when the card arrives; "restarting" is held until reload), showToast (voice idle auto-off and
      voice-app notices, warn), paintUpdateBanner (update available,
      persistent, Restart now focuses the upgrade card; closing hides it for
      that card) and ui/standing-feed.ts. A short CSS fade-in (styles.css
      .toast animation toast-in, set only under data-motion="full"), so
      reduced motion drops it.
    path: src/ui/toasts.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, design-system, toast, notice]
    tests:
      - test/toasts.test.ts
  gui-composer:
    description: >-
      #gui-composer (Atelier 2026-10-21, gnomon.voice.composer) - the
      composer wraps and grows with its text to 12 lines, then scrolls; the ⤢
      key toggles a tall view capped at 24 lines (persisted per viewer,
      gnomon.composer.tall); exactly one send control in the composer
      region. The controls sit in ONE row at the bottom right (line count,
      ⤢, send); the line count shows only from 2 lines up (lineCountShown),
      so the empty composer is one key tall (founder report 2026-10-23).
      Empty counts as one line whatever the placeholder (it stays on one
      line with an ellipsis), and the tall view gives back room the window
      lacks (fitTallRoom: send stays on screen, the conversation keeps 120 px,
      never under 12 lines) (Mika 2026-10-23).
      PURE core/composer.ts composerFit.
    path: src/core/composer.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, composer]
    tests:
      - test/voice-ladder.test.ts
      - test/dictation.test.ts
  gui-folder-field:
    description: >-
      #gui-folder-field (TD-2026-10-23-162; Atelier session
      2026-10-23-gnomon-folder-picker, design-system component folder-field,
      rule paths-are-chosen, migration batches folder-field and key-height).
      A folder or file on this Mac is CHOSEN, not typed. core/folder-field.ts
      (no DOM): FolderField controls one field over the kernel's
      request.folder.choose | check | recent (the kernel opens the macOS
      chooser, founder C1); every choice is checked before the key that uses
      it is enabled; the value sent is the kernel's real path and every path
      shown is the kernel's escaped display; the design copy (FF_COPY);
      fieldView draws recents (New session: up to six, the centre session's
      folder chosen else the most recent, C2, so cmd-N then Enter opens) or
      compact (Settings › Local model runner with "Use …/dist"; Mods › Add
      from folder; the file variant for Mods › Configure command). No drag
      from Finder (C3); the home folder is allowed with the amber warning
      (C4). ui/folder-field.ts draws it with h() (roving radios, arrows move
      and choose, Home/End, Enter submits the sheet) and routes data-ff-act
      presses (trusted only). The New session sheet is role=dialog with an
      h2, stays open (Opening…) until session.open answers and shows a
      refusal in place; every choice restores the folder's claude model
      (#gui-model-picker onFolder). styles.css carries the folder-field
      classes and --key-h (one key height, 28). Open-failed (setOpenFailed)
      may carry ONE key (data-ff-act error-key, trusted presses only; dropped
      with its error line). A changed claude binary (refusal.data.session
      claude_binary_changed, binaryChangedLine) says "Claude Code updated
      itself, so its binary no longer matches the one Gnomon pinned. next:
      review the re-pin card." with the key Review re-pin card when the
      refusal names its card, else the kernel's next and no key. The key
      holds the choice (keep) against THAT cardId (RepinReturn), closes the
      sheet and focuses the card; the store's card-outcome key for an allow
      reopens the sheet on the kept choice (restore) with Open focused, never
      opening the session; deny or expiry drops it.
    path: src/core/folder-field.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, atelier, paradigm-8, td-2026-10-23-162]
    tests:
      - test/folder-field.test.ts
      - test/mods.test.ts
      - test/desk.test.ts

  gui-local-model:
    description: >-
      #gui-local-model (TD-2026-10-22-769; Atelier session
      2026-10-22-gnomon-local-model, design-system settings-form, sheet
      section-focused, card family gnomon, alert refused-start, loop-detail
      cant_start). The Settings sheet's "Local model · kernel-owned" section
      between Voice and Permissions. core/local-model.ts (PURE): localStatusOf
      (status.local: not-connected | not-offered | windows | none | set),
      the form (setupForm, changeForm, pickServer fills the address only until
      typed), the page's checks (addressError: scheme, loopback host in lower
      case, port 1..65535, no path; model; endpoint name; runner path),
      probeRequest / setRequest / REMOVE_REQUEST, probeVerdict (C1 check-first:
      only an answer with the model listed raises the card), checkRowOf, the
      results (denied, expired, turned off) and toasts, localSection (every
      state, rows kinds readonly, form, request, term). ui/local-model.ts
      LocalModelController (no DOM): trusted presses only; one request at a
      time; Save = page checks (focus the first invalid field), then
      request.local.probe (rate-limited retry once), then request.local.config
      {op:'set'} (the card; focus Decide in the stack, which closes the sheet
      and focuses the card group, never Allow); the outcome from rows
      (approval.decide allow -> checking until status.local.lastProbe, a toast
      only when no sheet is open; deny / approval.expire / daemon.start -> the
      form returns with the entries and a "Not changed" line); Turn off =
      {op:'remove'}, an inline confirm only when loops use it (C2); Esc closes
      the confirm or form first. ui/settings-sheet.ts paints the section
      (heading "· kernel-owned" once, open(section) section-focused) and routes
      data-lm-act / data-lm-field / submit. core/render.ts localRowOf mirrors
      the kernel's and helper's gnomon-root-local:v1 row table (Aegis L4:
      runnerSource, port 1..65535, paths <= 256, no control or bidi characters,
      never compacted: a row whose helper line exceeds 1200 is refused) and
      localRootItems renders one line per signed field with the loop-diff marks
      on a change; the card head reads "⊙ gnomon". core/loops.ts startLine /
      cantStart / runRefusalOf: the loop detail's can't-start line per kernel
      why (none, sessions-only, no-runner, no-profile), Run now's reason, the
      needs-you pin and the refused-start alert key. Palette local.setup.
      Follow-ups: the Check row says "checking…" only from the kernel's
      status.local.probing (or a Check again in flight), "not checked yet"
      with Check again otherwise; Check again reads the refreshed
      status.local.lastProbe (the kernel records it), ui.check holds only a
      call that failed. A never-fired start refusal (count 0) is the same
      one alert, worded "■ <id> can’t start". settings-sheet.ts
      compositionGate: no repaint while an IME composition is active (owed,
      run at compositionend). The card's signed lines say their diff mark in
      sr-only "new: " / "was: " text (no aria-label on a list item).
      Tests: test/local-model.test.ts, test/root-rows.test.ts,
      test/loops-view.test.ts.
  gui-settings:
    description: >-
      #gui-settings (founder UI-first rule) - the header Day / Night / Auto
      theme switch and the Settings sheet (header gear key, Cmd-comma, the
      palette's "Settings..."). core/settings.ts is PURE: parseTheme /
      parseMotion (per-browser THEME_KEY / MOTION_KEY, like the Layout),
      themeSwitchEntries, unlockSeenOf (the cached unlock folded from
      kernel-principal approval.unlock / .dropped rows; daemon.start clears)
      and settingsModel (Appearance, Layout, Voice, Permissions, About). The
      sheet's theme row reads Day / Night / Auto without glyphs; the always-shown
      regions name "the browser risk chip" (never "badge" in copy). Every
      control names an existing GUI command in SETTINGS_RUNS (theme, motion,
      layout presets, pane toggles, workshop placement, mode.repo.*, voice app
      start/stop, voice.settings.open) or the standing Revoke
      (core/standing.ts revokeRequest); no new kernel verb. The Voice section
      only starts/stops the voice app, links the Voice settings sheet and
      reads out the rung in force (RUNG_NAME); everything voice configures
      lives in #gui-voice-settings. Kernel-owned values
      (mode ceiling, unlock and bounds, connection, bundle pin, the voice
      rung, the always-shown regions) are read-only rows with a how-to-change line,
      never a terminal-only path. ui/settings-sheet.ts paints with render.ts
      h() (text nodes, no inline style) and acts on trusted clicks only
      (G-GUI-04). settings.* is not block-safe. Aegis fixes: kernel rows are
      pinned to the connected home's kernel principal (standing.ts
      kernelPrincipalOf / isKernelPrincipal, also for the standing feed); an
      unseen unlock says only "no unlock seen since this page connected";
      run(id, trusted) carries the gesture's isTrusted from every path and the
      header switch checks it; the standing feed sits under overlays (hidden
      while a dialog is open), its offer is a toast (#gui-toast), and the stack
      pile reserves bottom room so today's list never covers a card key.
    path: src/core/settings.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, gui, settings, theme]
    tests:
      - test/settings.test.ts
      - test/voice-client.test.ts
